/lib-wrapper/
/pf-content/
/pf1-pow/
/pf1-psionics/
/pf1-statblock-converter/
/pf1spheres/
/statblock-library/
# sibling repos of this project, each with its own git root
/pf1-buff-bundles/
/pf1-buff-distributor/
/pf1-conditional-applier/

# ---- packs/ is SHIPPED CONTENT now, deliberately NOT ignored ----
#      This was `/pf1e_random_char_generator/packs/`, hiding a leftover LevelDB directory from the
#      removed spell-conditionals compendium, on the reasoning that module.json declared
#      "packs": [] so nothing there was distributed. That reasoning expired: the feat compendium
#      (tools/build_feat_pack.macro.js) lives there and IS declared and distributed.
#
#      Leaving it would have failed silently and twice -- the pack would never be committed, and
#      release.ps1 excluded packs/ from the zip for the same dead reason. Both were undone together,
#      because git and robocopy read different lists and a pack that works only on the authoring
#      machine is the worst shape this can take.
#
#      The DATA files (*.ldb, the numbered write-ahead *.log, CURRENT, MANIFEST-*) are committed.
#      These three are not: LOCK is a lock file Foundry holds open while a world is loaded -- git
#      cannot even read it then -- and LOG/LOG.old are LevelDB's own operational text. All three are
#      recreated on open, so shipping them is noise at best.
/pf1e_random_char_generator/packs/*/LOCK
/pf1e_random_char_generator/packs/*/LOG
/pf1e_random_char_generator/packs/*/LOG.old
